---
title: A sealed backend
summary: Why skoro's Backend trait is sealed to the burn backends it has been verified against.
order: 7
---

## Context

Every operation is implemented, and tested, against specific backends. A backend is more than
an interface: it has precision policies, device semantics and kernel coverage.

## Decision

`skoro_backend::Backend` is a subtrait of burn's backend with a private `Sealed` supertrait,
implemented only for `Flex` and `CubeBackend<R, F, I>`.

```rust
{../../../../crates/skoro-backend/src/lib.rs:17..32}
```

## Consequences

- Operation implementations can rely on the backends they were verified against.
- burn's autodiff decorators can't be passed in by accident.
- Adding a backend is a change to `skoro-backend`, not something a downstream crate can do.

> [!TODO]
> Is sealing about correctness (kernels per backend), about excluding `Autodiff<B>`, or both?
